# This repo tracks the PROCESS (scripts + docs), never image data. Raw frames,
# FITS/XISF intermediates, and stacked products are large and live OFF-REPO
# (backed up separately). Only per-dataset STATE (small JSON under
# datasets/<session>/<set>/) is versioned — see datasets/README.md.

# --- image data: raw frames, intermediates, products (any dir) ---
*.dng
*.DNG
*.nef
*.NEF
*.cr2
*.CR2
*.cr3
*.CR3
*.arw
*.ARW
*.raf
*.RAF
*.fit
*.fits
*.fts
*.xisf
*.ser
*.seq
*.tif
*.tiff
**/work/
**/results/

# --- anomaly-audit scratch ---
# audit_work/ (under datasets/<session>/<set>/) holds transient Siril working
# files — residual TIFFs, star lists, the .ssf, extracted-green FITS. ONLY the
# anomaly_audit.json record it contains is versioned; the rest is regenerated.
**/audit_work/*
!**/audit_work/anomaly_audit.json

# --- ingest scratch ---
# ingest_work/ (under datasets/<session>/<set>/) holds the pulled unit manifest
# and the sha256sum -c report. Only ingest.json — the transfer record — is
# versioned; the manifest and report are regenerated by re-running the fetch.
**/ingest_work/*
!**/ingest_work/ingest.json

# --- judgment surfaces (image data, never tracked) ---
**/judge/

# --- QA / calibration scratch ---
# qa_work/ (under datasets/<session>/<set>/) holds transient Siril working files
# (CFA FITS / .seq / .ssf / previews / logs). Only its .json records are versioned
# (frame_metrics.json, skyflat_qa.json, …); the rest is regenerated.
**/qa_work/*
!**/qa_work/*.json

# --- session data dirs (transient staging) ---
# Every acquisition session lives under sessions/<session>/ (raw lights +
# calibration + work/ intermediates). NEVER committed — one structural rule
# covers all sessions, no per-session entry needed.
#
# THIRD-PARTY practice corpora especially must never be committed or
# redistributed — download and PROCESS only, link the source (terms vary: some
# are CC-BY-NC-SA / no-redistribute). Record each one's source + license in a
# comment here when one is staged.
/sessions/

# --- the OBSERVING SITE (a home address) — LOCAL ONLY, never tracked ---
# The real coordinates live in site.local.json: rig-local under scripts/setup/,
# session-local under sessions/<session>/ (which /sessions/ above already
# covers). The chain reads them through scripts/lib/acquisition.py and writes NO
# coordinate into any tracked record — acquisition.json's `site` block carries
# the config's sha256 + provenance only. The tracked template is
# scripts/setup/site.example.json (null values). scripts/qa/check_site_privacy.py
# goes RED on any form of the value (decimal, sexagesimal, geocentric, a numeric
# `site` block) in the tree or the index. Owner-directed: the site had reached 23
# tracked files (docs/dead-ends/evidence-provenance.md, "THE OBSERVING SITE IS A HOME ADDRESS").
**/site.local.json

# --- durable outputs (web-servable, image data — never tracked) ---
# web/ itself is TRACKED (the front-end code + assets); its results/ data
# tree is not. The `**/results/` pattern above already ignores web/results/;
# this line makes the contract explicit.
/web/results/

# --- vendor tool payloads staged at the repo root ---
# Downloaded installer archives + model weights. Multi-GB binaries and image
# data: never committed, never redistributed (vendor licences vary). The tool
# itself installs to /opt and is recorded in scripts/setup/manifest.tsv — this
# dir is only the staging area the archives were fetched into.
/cosmic/

# --- tooling / OS cruft ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# --- root-level images are working screenshots (judgment surfaces), never data ---
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg

# disto_work/ (under datasets/<session>/<set>/) holds the displacement-field
# probe's transient files (converted FITS, warped TIFFs, darktable/siril logs,
# the .ssf). Only the JSON record and the two reproducers are versioned.
**/disto_work/*
!**/disto_work/*.json
!**/disto_work/displacement_field_probe.py
!**/disto_work/warp_ab.sh

# starlight_work/ (under datasets/<session>/<set>/) holds the starlight-
# preservation instrument's records plus the background-arm surfaces it
# measures. The JSON records are the evidence and are versioned — including
# gaia_cells_cache.json, which is the catalogue side of every number in them
# and is what reproduces a run offline (`--offline --cache=<that file>`; an arm
# also inherits it from its `--baseline`'s directory). The arm .fit files
# are derived image data (the blanket *.fit rule already excludes them).
**/starlight_work/*
!**/starlight_work/*.json

# smear_work/ (under datasets/<session>/) holds the compose-smear re-march's
# Siril star lists and its .ssf. The JSON carries the tool's own medians per
# position, which is the record; the .lst files are the intermediate it derived
# them from and are not versioned (qa_work/starlight_work pattern, not psf_work's).
**/smear_work/*
!**/smear_work/*.json

# psf_work/ (under datasets/<session>/<set>/) holds the raw-frame PSF-field
# probe's Siril star lists and its .ssf. The .lst files ARE the record.
**/psf_work/*
!**/psf_work/*.lst

# corner_work/pa_sample_a/ — record (a)'s 18 findstar lists, REBUILT FROM GIT by
# pa_convention.py rather than copied: 9 are still tracked under psf_work/ and
# all 18 are in ba9a7ff, the commit that made the claim. Tracking them here would
# duplicate 136k lines and make a git ref look like a copy.
datasets/aug06/corner_work/pa_sample_a/

# corner_work/psf_calib_work/ — the synthetic trailed-star FIXTURES (43 MB of
# rendered frames) and Siril's star lists over them. Regenerated in full by
# psf_calib.py; the tracked record is psf_calib.json.
datasets/aug06/corner_work/psf_calib_work/

# drift_work/ — the per-frame drift-bearing probe. 3.3 GB of staged raws and
# debayered frames; the .lst star lists and the .ssf ARE the record and are kept,
# and drift_bearing.py rebuilds everything else from sessions/.
**/drift_work/*
!**/drift_work/*.lst
!**/drift_work/*.ssf

# dtseries_work/ — the series run that verified the quadrature assumption. Full
# sensor frames and TIFFs are regenerable; the .lst records and .ssf are kept.
**/dtseries_work/*
!**/dtseries_work/*.lst
!**/dtseries_work/*.ssf

# dtresample_work/ — the darktable half of the resample-cost probe. Synthetic
# frames and TIFFs (98-294 MB each) are regenerable; the .lst star lists and the
# .ssf ARE the record.
**/dtresample_work/*
!**/dtresample_work/*.lst
!**/dtresample_work/*.ssf

# resample_work/ — the resample-cost probe. Synthetic frames, registered copies
# and siril logs are regenerable; the .lst star lists and the .ssf ARE the record.
**/resample_work/*
!**/resample_work/*.lst
!**/resample_work/*.ssf

# memraw_work/ — the member-versus-constituent-raws test. Staged raws and
# debayered frames are regenerable; the .lst records and .ssf are the record.
**/memraw_work/*
!**/memraw_work/*.lst
!**/memraw_work/*.ssf

# inject_work/ — synthetic trails injected into a real frame. The injected FITS is
# image DATA and stays out. THE SITE ARRAYS ARE NOT REGENERABLE and an earlier
# version of this comment said they were: no tracked script injects, and no seed
# is recorded in the ledger, so the injector died with its session. sites*.npy is
# the ONLY surviving ground truth for which detections are planted and which are
# real — i.e. the label without which the positive control that exonerated the
# coherent-term estimator cannot be re-run. 44 KB each, a record not image data.
**/inject_work/*
!**/inject_work/*.lst
!**/inject_work/*.ssf
!**/inject_work/sites*.npy

# skyrate_work/ — the scalar-vs-projection refit of the sky-rate coefficient.
# The member star list IS the record; the .ssf reproduces it.
**/skyrate_work/*
!**/skyrate_work/*.lst
!**/skyrate_work/*.ssf

# ca_work/ — the C/A and july27 exposure-lever probe. Staged raws and debayered
# frames are regenerable; the .lst star lists and the .ssf ARE the record.
**/ca_work/*
!**/ca_work/*.lst
!**/ca_work/*.ssf

# bearing_work/ — the per-set drift-bearing probe. Staged raws, debayered frames
# and siril logs are regenerable; the .lst star lists and the .ssf ARE the record.
**/bearing_work/*
!**/bearing_work/*.lst
!**/bearing_work/*.ssf

# astroreg_work/ — the astrometric-registration probe's sequence files. Only the
# .seq (the registration data it produced) and the .ssf are worth keeping.
**/astroreg_work/*
!**/astroreg_work/*.seq
!**/astroreg_work/*.ssf

# compose_ab/ — the astrometric-vs-star-pair compose A/B. Only the star lists,
# the box coordinates and the .ssf are the record; the stacks are regenerable.
**/compose_ab/*
!**/compose_ab/*.lst
!**/compose_ab/*.ssf
!**/compose_ab/*.txt

# union_ab/ — the 28-member union A/B. Star lists, scripts and box coordinates
# are the record; the unions and registered copies are regenerable.
**/union_ab/*
!**/union_ab/*.lst
!**/union_ab/*.ssf
!**/union_ab/*.txt

# flatdiff_work/ (under datasets/<session>/<set>/) holds the flat-differential
# A/B's Siril star lists, .ssf, psf logs and split channel planes. Only the JSON
# records are versioned; the rest is regenerated by re-running the arms and
# scripts/qa/flat_differential.py.
**/flatdiff_work/*
!**/flatdiff_work/*.json

# pergroup_work/ (under datasets/<session>/<set>/) holds the flat-window arms'
# per-pair Siril working dirs — split channel planes, star lists, .ssf, psf logs
# and the cropped ratio windows. Only the JSON records are versioned; the rest is
# regenerated by re-running the arms, scripts/qa/flat_differential.py,
# scripts/qa/flat_odd_component.py and scripts/qa/grid_ramp.py.
# Records land in pergroup_work/ ITSELF, never in a subdirectory: git does not
# descend into an excluded directory, so a negation inside one cannot re-include
# anything (`!**/pergroup_work/window/*.json` silently matches nothing).
**/pergroup_work/*
!**/pergroup_work/*.json

# tilt_work/ (under datasets/<session>/<set>/) holds the object-tilt instrument's
# Siril star lists, .ssf and psf logs. Only the JSON record is versioned; the
# rest is regenerated by re-running scripts/qa/object_tilt.py.
**/tilt_work/*
!**/tilt_work/*.json

# psfex_work/ — the PSFEx head-to-head. Green-plane frames and LDAC catalogues
# are regenerable (Siril split + source-extractor); the .psf field models, the
# configs and the logs ARE the record.
**/psfex_work/*
!**/psfex_work/*.psf
!**/psfex_work/*.sex
!**/psfex_work/*.param
!**/psfex_work/*.ssf
!**/psfex_work/*.xml
!**/psfex_work/*.log
!**/psfex_work/deg*/

# phot_work/ — the catalogue-referenced photometry probe. Staged frames, siril
# logs and star lists are regenerable by re-running the .ssf; only the generated
# scripts and the JSON records ARE the record.
**/phot_work/*
!**/phot_work/*.json
!**/phot_work/*.py
!**/phot_work/*.ssf
!**/phot_work/*.lst
!**/phot_work/*.corr

# kappa_work/ — the kappa-transfer fixture: four arms x 15 synthetic 1200x1200
# frames plus their Siril star lists and logs, 170 MB, ALL of it regenerable by
# re-running kappa_transfer.py (which is tracked, as is its JSON record). Ignored
# WHOLLY, following psf_calib_work/: a synthetic fixture's intermediates are not
# records, and the 4.3 MB of star lists are derived from tracked code alone.
datasets/aug06/corner_work/kappa_work/

# frames_work/ — the 40-frame depth arm: hard-linked raws, 40 debayered FITS
# (~5.9 GB) and their Siril star lists, all regenerable from measure.ssf and the
# tracked frame_map.json. Only the map, the script and the JSON record ARE the
# record.
**/frames_work/*
!**/frames_work/*.json
!**/frames_work/*.ssf

# cfa_work/ — the CFA control: undebayered FITS, four split_cfa channels per
# frame and their star lists, all regenerable from measure_cfa.ssf and
# frames_work/frame_map.json. Only the script and the JSON records ARE the record.
**/cfa_work/*
!**/cfa_work/*.json
!**/cfa_work/*.ssf

# sirilpy_work/ (under datasets/<session>/<set>/) holds the analyse_image_from_file
# probe. The debayered FITS (1.7 GB for 12 frames) are derived data and are deleted
# after the run; the generated .ssf carry ABSOLUTE paths and are recorded inside the
# JSON instead of tracked, so nothing machine-local enters the tree. The probe script
# and the records ARE the record.
**/sirilpy_work/*
!**/sirilpy_work/*.json
!**/sirilpy_work/*.py

# --- measurement-evidence dirs under datasets/ (crop5lr + corpus sweeps) ---
# The tracked RECORD of a measurement is its JSON summary (instrument + inputs
# + exact command + the tool's own numbers); bulk findstar .lst output is
# EVIDENCE and retires to git history when its route closes (recovery:
# `git show 2654d31:<path>`, aug06 within-night arc `git show 6d9e568:<path>`;
# resolvers indexed in datasets/corpus/README.md). These dirs once tracked
# 615 .lst (76.8 MB) BY DEFAULT because no block existed here — a new *_work/
# dir gets its block BEFORE its first commit.
# crop5lr cross-night A/B evidence (route RETIRED; the engagement's JSON
# records at crop_work/ top level stay tracked):
datasets/corpus/crop_work/*/
# ledger-cited probe dirs whose small records ARE the content (dir-level
# negation per the pergroup_work rule above — negating files INSIDE an
# excluded dir matches nothing; negating the DIR itself lets git descend):
!datasets/corpus/crop_work/memprobe/
!datasets/corpus/crop_work/setq/
# corpus rebuild verification sweeps (route KEPT; corpus_sweep_{old,new}.json
# are the ledger-cited records; lists regenerable while the products live):
datasets/corpus/corpus_sweep_old/
datasets/corpus/corpus_sweep_new/
# within-night crop5 A/B evidence (route NULL/closed; its top-level JSONs stay):
datasets/aug06/crop_work/*/
# pedestal zero-point investigation (route OPEN; ledger
# pedestal_8pct_hypothesis_C_output_norm_minmax): the record is the JSON + the
# arithmetic deriving (mu, D) from Siril's own seqstat / .seq M-line numbers;
# the seqstat CSVs are the instrument's raw reading (40-115 lines each) and
# the hand .ssf are the exact commands — kept. Registered r_ copies, kept
# compose scratches and products never enter (they live under web/results/).
datasets/corpus/pedestal_work/*
!datasets/corpus/pedestal_work/*.json
!datasets/corpus/pedestal_work/*.py
!datasets/corpus/pedestal_work/*.csv
!datasets/corpus/pedestal_work/*.ssf
# datasets/corpus/campaign_zeropoint/ — the output-norm-zero-point from-raws
# campaign (BACKLOG:output-norm-zero-point; ledger aug06
# output_norm_zero_point_campaign_from_raws). The RECORD is tracked: the driver
# (.sh), the move-aside manifest, the unchecked premises, campaign_record.json
# and readout_scripts/*.py (the diagnostics every count and table in the record
# came from — tracked so the sha256 the record quotes resolves to text).
# readout_work/ is the readouts' scratch and tracks nothing: symlink sequences
# + Siril .ssf/logs/CSVs, the per-tier JSON intermediates the record was
# assembled from, and the eye-inspection panels (~120 MB of 8-bit PNGs derived
# from the 16-bit judge surfaces) — reproducible from the scripts on the
# products, none a deliverable.
datasets/corpus/campaign_zeropoint/readout_work/
